Here is the complete, unified Master Optimization & Compatibility Checklist for InvictusOS, combining every previous fix with the new CSS, layout, and UX improvements.

1. Architecture & Reverse Progressive Loading

• Adopt 1-Tier Reverse Progressive Loading: Serve a lightweight base.css (~8 KB) by default so 2000s browsers and 256 MB PCs load instantaneously, and use a 6-line ES3-safe JavaScript gatekeeper to inject animations.css and effects.js only on modern hardware (>= 2 GB RAM).
• Add a 25 FPS Auto-Kill Watchdog: Have effects.js monitor frame rate for the first 2 seconds and automatically unload animations.css if a weak modern laptop drops below 25 FPS.
• Stick to ES3 JavaScript in Inline Scripts: Only use var and function() (no const, let, or arrow functions) in your inline <script> inside index.html so IE6 and Firefox 2 never throw syntax popups.
• Delete simplesite/ and Both Switch to Simple Site Links: Once your 1-tier progressive setup is live, remove the redundant simplesite/ folder, the insulting "This PC looks low-end" banner, the popup modal, and both duplicate Switch to Simple Site links.

2. CSS & Legacy Browser Fallbacks (2000s PC Safe)

• Declare Solid Background Colors Before Gradients: Always write a flat hex background-color right above any linear-gradient or rgba() rule so 2000s browsers never render invisible white-on-white text.
• Gate or Tile Graph/Grid Backgrounds: Keep heavy CSS repeating-linear-gradient grid backgrounds inside animations.css so old CPUs don't lag while scrolling, or use a tiny 16×16 .gif/.png tile image (~150 bytes) in base.css.
• Add inline-block / Block Fallbacks Before CSS Grid & Flexbox: Write standard inline-block or block stacking rules before @supports (display: grid) so your 4 stat cards (512 MB, 5 GB, 900 MHz, NO) don't collapse into a broken pile on IE6 and Firefox 2.
• Pair px Fallbacks with rem Units: Always declare px font sizes and spacing before rem (font-size: 16px; font-size: 1rem;) so early browsers calculate text sizes accurately.
• Use 1px Solid Borders in base.css: Replace CPU-heavy box-shadow and backdrop-filter blurs in the base stylesheet with clean 1px solid borders.
• Avoid 100vh Hero Heights: Use standard top/bottom padding instead of height: 100vh so the primary Download button is never pushed off-screen on 640×480 or 1024×600 netbook displays.

3. Assets, Fonts & Media

• Delete Heavy & Unused Images: Remove desktop.png (784 KB) and all five uncompressed .png team portraits (736 KB).
• Use <picture> with JPEG/PNG Fallbacks: Pair desktop.webp (42 KB) with a compressed desktop.jpg (~30 KB) fallback, and add a .png fallback for logo.svg so 2000s browsers display your branding properly.
• Keep Images Fluid Without Layout Shifts: Add explicit width and height attributes to every <img> tag alongside img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; } in CSS.
• Move Custom Fonts into animations.css: Load your 8 .woff2 font files (243 KB) only inside animations.css so legacy PCs render built-in system fonts (Arial, Courier New) with zero download delay.
• Add a Root favicon.ico: Place a tiny 1 KB favicon.ico in your root folder so stock 2000s browsers stop throwing silent 404 errors looking for it.

4. Navigation, HTML Hygiene & Copywriting

• Put <meta charset="UTF-8"> First in <head>: Place the charset tag at the very top of <head> so older browsers don't garble characters like × (640×480) or —.
• Fix Broken Icon Ligatures & Duplicate Alt-Text: Replace leaking ligature text (iv Available, 32 Available) with clean HTML badges (<span class="badge">Available</span>), and fix screen-reader duplicates ("Lightweight | Fast | Reliable Lightweight, fast, reliable" and "IDEA ---> EXECUTION Idea to execution").
• Remove the Header Animations Button & Add Anchor Links: Keep the top navigation bar clean with essential links (Requirements, Features, Installation, FAQ, Download) plus quick jump anchors (#requirements, #download) for easy navigation on 640×480 screens.
• Wire Up Footer Legal/Support Links: Turn the plain-text Privacy Terms Support footer items into working <a href="/privacy/">, <a href="/terms/">, and <a href="/support/"> links, and unify the exact same header and footer across every page (index.html, 404.html, download/, faq/, etc.).
• Standardize Hardware Specs: Use identical numbers everywhere (900 MHz CPU / 512 MB RAM / 5 GB storage minimum; 1 GHz CPU / 1 GB RAM / 15 GB storage recommended; 640×480 minimum display).
• Use Minimal, Honest Team Credits: Drop portraits, paragraph bios, and inflated titles (Software Architect, Head of Marketing, Webmaster) in favor of plain names and simple two-word labels (Core Development, Testing & Development, Design, Support & Docs, Web).
• Add ISO File Size & SHA256 Checksum: Display the exact .iso download size and verification hash right below the download button.

5. Hosting & Repository Cleanup

• Allow Plain http:// Access on Cloudflare: Connect a custom domain to Cloudflare Pages and disable "Always Use HTTPS" under SSL/TLS → Edge Certificates so stock 2000s browsers aren't blocked by modern TLS 1.2/1.3 encryption errors.
• Keep Source Clean & Auto-Minify on Edge: Keep GitHub source files readable and well-commented, letting Cloudflare Pages handle CSS/HTML minification automatically on deploy.
• Delete Dead Repo Files: Remove oldindex.html, download/oldindex.html, for hosted fonts, and todo from the repository.
